@coderabbitai Valid. Fixed in a571fc60d9.

On updown's "Warn about expiring domain names" feature page, the founder says the reminders were "released (disabled by default …), feel free to enable it for your account". The API has no account-settings endpoint; updown's "Settings API for account level configuration" request is still open. The helper therefore cannot turn the reminders on.

The guide now has a once-per-account step before "Set up a site": enable domain-expiration reminders in the updown.io account settings. The Quick Reference "Not in the API" line now lists account settings, including these reminders (off by default), next to the custom domain. The private, hourly check setup is unchanged.

